{ga .i'amsi} requires the pause, if I'm not mistaken. It seems as easy to distinguish {gai'amsi} from {ga .i'amsi} as {dai} from {da .i}. 


On Sunday, January 18, 2015 at 3:07 AM, John Cowan wrote:

> Alex Burka scripsit:
> 
> > > {gai'amsi} doesn't have a consonant cluster in the first five letters after 
> > > removing y'y and ybu.
> > > 
> > 
> > 
> > This is true, but even with no cluster there is nowhere for it to
> > break up (since y'ybu can't start or end a word and -ms- is not an
> > initial cluster). So, at least under camxes, it is a zi'evla.
> > 
> 
> 
> Nevertheless, that consonant cluster is a requirement. In any case,
> it can't be distinguished from "ga i'amsi" in writing, though
> different in speech.
> 
> Some sequences are just junk, and that's all there is to them.
> 
